     "text": "{\"cost\": 4, \"rationale\": \"Entry footholds are free starting points, so they are not counted as steps. One shortest path is: memoryDump:credentialAccess (from phishing or exposedApi), then jumpHost:lateralMovement, then shareMount:collection, then crownData:exfiltrate, for 4 steps. A 3-step path is impossible. It would need a collection step reachable in 2 steps, which means its parent would have to be reachable in 1 step directly from an entry. The candidate parents (jumpHost, fileServer, monitoringHost, backupHost, secretsManager, serviceAccount, domainAdmin) all need at least one intermediate step first.\"}"
